@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-c-api C API
@brief There is no C API; C code is tested from C++.

@details
µTest++ is built on C++20 features, such as templates, concepts, and
lambdas, which have no equivalent in C, so it has no C API.

To test C code, write the test cases in C++ and call the C functions from
them. If the C headers do not declare their functions with `extern "C"`
themselves, include them in an `extern "C"` block:

@code{.cpp}
extern "C"
{
#include "adder.h"
}

ts.test ("Check the C adder", [] (auto& t) {
  t.expect (mt::eq (add (2, 3), 5));
});
@endcode
